## Colors

| Token | Value | Intended use |
|---|---|---|
| `colors.primary` | `#2563EB` | primary actions, active states |
| `colors.secondary` | `#0F172A` | headings, high-emphasis text |
| `colors.neutral` | `#64748B` | secondary text, borders |
| `colors.success` | `#15803D` | confirmation |
| `colors.warning` | `#B45309` | recoverable problems |
| `colors.danger` | `#B91C1C` | destructive actions, errors |

Every foreground/background pair used in a component must pass the ratios in **Accessibility** below.

## Typography

Most design systems have 9–15 levels. Define each with its role, not just its size.

| Level | Role |
|---|---|
| `display-lg` | page hero |
| `headline-md` | section heading |
| `body-md` | default body copy |
| `label-sm` | form labels, metadata |

## Layout

Grid, margins, safe areas, and the spacing scale. Spacing uses the `spacing.*` tokens exclusively —
