## Do's and Don'ts

- **Do** reference tokens by name. **Don't** hardcode a hex value in a component.
- **Do** define a new token when a value repeats three times. **Don't** invent one-off values.
- **Do** keep contrast pairs inside the ratios below. **Don't** ship a pair the linter flags.

<!-- Extensions below. Not yet covered by the design.md alpha spec. -->

## Motion

Durations and easings, typed as DTCG `duration` and `cubicBezier` so they survive token export.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `motion.instant` | 100ms | state feedback |
| `motion.fast` | 180ms | hovers, small transitions |
| `motion.base` | 240ms | panel and sheet entry |
| `motion.ease-standard` | `[0.2, 0, 0, 1]` | default easing |

Honour `prefers-reduced-motion` by reducing to opacity-only transitions.

## Breakpoints

| Name | Min width | Layout behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| sm | 480px | single column |
| md | 768px | two column, persistent nav |
| lg | 1200px | three column, sidebar visible |

## States

Every interactive component defines all eight: **default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled,
loading, error, empty**. `focus-visible` must remain visible — never remove the focus ring without
supplying a replacement with at least 3:1 contrast against the adjacent surface.

## Accessibility

- Body text contrast at least **4.5:1**; large text (18pt, or 14pt bold) at least **3:1**.
- Computed ratios are **not rounded** — 4.499:1 fails.
- Non-text contrast is governed separately; keep UI component boundaries at 3:1 or better.
- The `contrast-ratio` lint rule enforces the component pairs above; CI runs it.

## Token Export

```bash
npx @google/design.md lint DESIGN.md
npx @google/design.md export --format dtcg        > tokens.json
npx @google/design.md export --format css-tailwind > src/styles/tokens.css
```

`tokens.json` is W3C Design Tokens Format Module output, so the tokens remain portable if this file
is ever retired.
